    },
    "message": "Give each branch of a Run its own writer lease and status\n\nclaim_branch locks a branch's own worker-lock after taking the Run's gate\nfor a moment, so writers of different branches work at once. claim_run,\nfor operations on a whole Run, holds the gate and refuses while any branch\nis written. Only exclusive locks are used, as Windows offers. Each branch\nrecords its computation status in its own status.json, version 1; the\nRun's status becomes their summary. Recovery interrupts branches left\nrunning without a writer and forgets the status of a fork's child that\nwas never created.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
